      "role": "duck",
      "text": "So you're seeing 50.98 instead of 50.97. What part of the rounding logic in the invoice file are you looking at first?"
    },
    {
      "role": "you",
      "text": "I've got an invoice test failing, the total comes out as 50.98, but the test expects 50.97."
    },
    {
      "role": "duck",
      "text": "Got it, 50.98 instead of 50.97. Does that difference happen before or after the discount is applied?"
    },
    {
      "role": "you",
      "text": "I think the discount gets rounded for each item and then added up, so each item rounds up a little."
    },
    {
      "role": "duck",
      "text": "Rounding each item individually. What would happen if you summed the discounts before rounding?"
    },
    {
      "role": "you",
      "text": "I haven't checked that yet. The test passes the disk out as a float, not a decimal, which might matter too."
    },
    {
